        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I appreciate the imposters feature being available. Anyone uploading an avatar with 17 outfits on it while they only ever use one should absolutely be subjected to the pixel hell that is imposters on my side. Sometimes, it does do a decent approximation of the person's actual avatar.\n\nHowever... the imposter often doesn't represent the actual avatar being worn exactly because of those toggles. Shader colouring, different outfits, hair styles, etc...\n\nAnd being interacted with by an imposter is like watching a cardboard cutout soaked in water and then re-dried reach out to your head and try to headpat you due to the lack of hand gestures and other bone movements.\n\nSo, as has been suggested before, uploaders should be able to upload a custom fallback and assign it to specific avatars, while disabling fallbacks entirely for those avatars. That way, the uploader has confidence that they will be seen in a way that truly represents them.\n\nPerhaps a friendly callout to users in the SDK that making a fallback obvious via badge, wristband, writing on shirt, etc... could even be warranted, too. But I know that that'd be a stretch.\n\nI can understand and agree that imposters may provide a better experience than fallbacks for those that don't upload their own avatars. But for people that do, fallbacks can provide a much better experience and should be kept. Improved even, as requested above.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
