      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It seems that creating custom fallbacks is no longer possible, despite docs.vrchat.com still outlining the process, and the SDK still providing a notice of whether an avatar is elligible as a fallback or not.\n\nAdditionally, the creative possibilities with custom fallbacks far outweigh their removal in my opinion. Although I am not aware of VRC's tech, I don't see how the removal of this system simplifies anything given the existing complexity and reuse of similar systems (presumably) by impostors. Impostors are a great low-effort workaround to performance blocking, however, on all platform, enough effort from an avatar creator can pretty much always lead to something 90% of the way to the full-spec avatar, while fitting in the Good ranks.\n\nI've just discovered it's now impossible to select a custom avatar that satisfies the fallback requirements of good or better on all platforms, and spent time searching why the button to select it was unavailable. I cannot find anywhere saying this feature was removed; only that it's not possible to select them from the in-game UI.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-06-02T21:01:55.449Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please don't do that. Imposters are nice, but a lot of us enjoy having the novelty of creating nicer, more professional looking avatars. A lot of us have already spent hours of time making them.\n\nIf anything, make it a VRC+ feature, to allow users to upload their own custom \"imposter\" avatars, aka fallbacks, within performance limitations.",
